  "decision": "No supported >=90% identity-preserving mapping for the whole Governing Configuration subject. Project.Settings and its carrier are distinct from default settings and may not encompass routing/customization or structured claim content. Current body evidence gives no unified definition or subtype relationships for the old label. Per-source Subject replacements require separate supported targets and scope review after the conceptual decision.",
  "question": "Should Governing Configuration remain a distinct MODEL concept covering authoritative configuration beyond Project.Settings (including defaults, routing and customization), or should it be retired and each source governed by its specific existing target?",
  "blast_radius": "Seven active-target sources (R1441, R1429, R1226, R1640, R1641, D407, D408), plus passive dependencies and R1200 Claim-carrier wording in the pinned non-Workbench/non-Workflow source list. Actual instance migration and other agents\u2019 Workbench/Workflow scopes are not assessed. Project.Settings merge remains intact; carrier/default/override precedence must be preserved.",
